parts+=['<h2>Measured cost and its limits</h2>',image('performance.png','Median of three released-step medians per mode. D: and C: measurements are explicitly separate.'),table(['Profile','Off median µs','Full median µs','Full/off'],[(label,f"{r['timings'][key]['off']['medianOfMediansUs']:.1f}",f"{r['timings'][key]['full']['medianOfMediansUs']:.1f}",f"{r['timings'][key]['overheadRatio']:.3f}×") for label,key in [('Baseline D:','baseline'),('Optimized prototype D:','prototypeSameDrive'),('Final build C:','optimized')]]),'<p>The matched D: coast medians fell from 77.6 to 72.7 µs (6.3%). That prototype precedes the final flush-schedule repair. Final C: coast results establish the current same-build full/off ratio; cross-volume comparisons cannot isolate an algorithmic speedup. Each coast used 2 s settle + 3 s released motion, 5 m/s launch, three interleaved fresh-process repeats, OpenGL and two scheduled native screenshots. Continuous visual capture and browser UI were excluded from these budget runs.</p>',image('phases.png','Actual opt-in 10,000-step diagnostic. The solver/attribution span includes native job waits, with profiling clock overhead included.'),'<p>Off retains native trial control and the declared common probe; it is not an unmodified upstream baseline. The probe measures steady-clock step elapsed time, includes enabled ledger reduction/copy, and excludes its own sampling/queueing. The CRC microbenchmark processed 65,536,000 bytes per repeat; median byte-table time was 128.211 ms versus 30.771 ms for slicing by eight. This is a checksum benchmark, not an end-to-end simulation speedup.</p>']
parts+=['<h2>Slow-disk drain findings</h2>',image('drain.png','Final corrected D: recorder progress, independently polled while the native writers drained.'),table(['D: barrier run','Step median µs','Worker wall s','Detail sync calls'],[('Original baseline','107.5',f"{before['barrier']['workerWallSeconds']:.1f}",'not instrumented'),('Pre-cadence prototype','102.5',f"{proto['barrier']['workerWallSeconds']:.1f}",'70'),('Final corrected build',f"{dr['stepMedianUs']:.1f}",f"{dr['workerWallSeconds']:.1f}",dr['recorder']['syncCalls'])]),'<p>The prototype exposed a feedback loop: reset-before-sync made a slow flush immediately trigger another flush. The repair reduced 70 synchronization calls to 10 on these individual runs. Final D: wall time was 60.2 s, versus 91.3 s for the instrumented prototype and 52.9 s for the original baseline. Thus this evidence does not establish a general end-to-end speedup over the original build. Disk variability, shared I/O, and one run per detail variant limit that claim. The final C: barrier took '+f"{now['barrier']['workerWallSeconds']:.1f}"+' s on a different volume; it is not a matched-drive algorithm comparison.</p>', '<p>One final D: synchronization blocked for '+f"{dr['recorder']['maxSyncWallUs']/1e6:.2f}"+' s. Peak queue occupancy was 13,734 / 15,709 frames (87.4%). The separate ~3 GiB queue and 820,429,056-byte history reservation remain necessary. Producer copy traffic fell from 4,921,344,000 to 3,102,745,920 bytes; raw window payload remained 1,550,318,264 bytes. No rates, required windows, coverage thresholds or resource preflight floors were reduced.</p>']
